# Practical 02 - Angular Components

## Aim

To create and use components in an Angular application.

## Introduction

A component is a basic building block of an Angular application.

A component contains:

- HTML for the user interface
- CSS for styling
- TypeScript for the logic

## Software Used

- Angular
- TypeScript
- HTML
- CSS
- Visual Studio Code

## Procedure

### Step 1: Create an Angular Project

Open Command Prompt or Terminal and type:

ng new component-demo

### Step 2: Open the Project

cd component-demo

### Step 3: Create a Component

Run:

ng generate component student

or

ng g c student

### Step 4: Write Component Code

The component files are created automatically.

The main files are:

- student.component.ts
- student.component.html
- student.component.css
- student.component.spec.ts

### Step 5: Add HTML Code

In `student.component.html`, write:

<h2>Student Information</h2>

<p>Name: Aarti Navnath Tonpe</p>

<p>Course: M.Sc. Computer Science</p>

### Step 6: Run the Application

Run:

ng serve --open

## Expected Output

The browser displays:

Student Information

Name: Aarti Navnath Tonpe

Course: M.Sc. Computer Science

## Result

The Angular component was successfully created and displayed in the application.

## Conclusion

Thus, an Angular component was successfully created and used in an Angular application.
